\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The determinant at two quaternionic links}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{For #{U=\qi}, #{V=\qj}, the variables of
\ref{fdip-00ZD} are #{a=-1-\qi}, #{b=-1-\qj}.
Their norms are both #{2}, and #{ab-ba=2\qk}, so
#{s=4} and #{t=4}. At mass #{5},
##{\det K_{\qi,\qj}(5)
=\bigl((25-4)^2-4\bigr)^4=437^4.}
The identity pair instead has #{s=t=0} and determinant
#{625^4=5^{16}}, agreeing with \ref{fdip-00ZB}.}
